# =============================================================================
# SEA-Net -- what does NOT go on GitHub
#
# The rule: commit everything needed to REPRODUCE and UNDERSTAND the work, and
# nothing that is large, machine-specific, or regenerated by running a command.
#
#   committed : code, configs, guides, and the curated results
#               (results.csv, leaderboard, comparison tables, training history,
#                figures, real run logs)
#   ignored   : datasets, model weights, the MLflow store, raw prediction
#               arrays, smoke output, caches, editor and OS noise
#
# IMPORTANT: adding a path here does NOT remove a file that git already tracks.
# For that you need `git rm -r --cached <path>` once; the file stays on disk.
# =============================================================================

# --- Editor / OS noise -------------------------------------------------------
*~
*#
*.swp
*.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
/.idea/
# The VS Code folder is personal EXCEPT launch.json, which is the shared debug config
# (see guide/13_debugging.md). A negation only works if the parent folder is not excluded,
# which is why this is "/.vscode/*" and not "/.vscode/".
/.vscode/*
!/.vscode/launch.json

# --- Python ------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/
/.coverage
/.coverage.*
/.cache
/.pytest_cache
/.mypy_cache
/build
/dist
.ipynb_checkpoints/
# virtual environments, whatever they are called locally
/.venv/
/venv/
/env/

# --- Secrets -----------------------------------------------------------------
# The Telegram bot token + chat id used for phone notifications from Grid5000.
# scripts/telegram_secrets.example.sh IS committed; the real one never is.
scripts/telegram_secrets.sh
*.env
.env

# =============================================================================
# BIG OR REGENERABLE
# =============================================================================

# The datasets: the UCR 2018 archive (~850 MB, its own licence) and the
# synthetic WebTraffic csvs. See guide/02_datasets.md for how to fetch them.
/data/

# Saved model weights: large, and regenerated by training.
/model/
*.pth
*.pt
*.ckpt

# The MLflow store. A database in git bloats the history and conflicts on every
# merge; copy it off the training machine with scp instead, or point both
# machines at one server with MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI. See guide/09_mlflow.md.
/mlflow.db
/mlflow*.db
/mlruns/
/mlartifacts/

# Optuna's own study database, when a search is run with storage on disk.
/optuna*.db

# Raw per-series probability arrays (~30 MB). Only scripts/ensemble_vote.py
# reads them, and its OUTPUT (ensemble_vote.csv) is committed, so the arrays
# themselves are not worth the space. The ** covers both results roots
# (results/old_results/SEA_NET/... and results/top_results/SEA_NET/...).
results/**/predictions/

# Smoke-test output. `--smoke` runs are throwaway 3-epoch pipeline checks.
# Real training output IS committed, so a run's record travels with the repo.
results/**/logs/smoke/
results/**/interpretation/*/smoke/
/results/_selftest/

# TorchScript and ONNX exports inside a deploy/ bundle. They are REGENERATED from
# the committed <stem>.pt (weights + config) by seanet/deployment.py, so keeping
# them out saves ~3 MB per model without losing anything. The .pt, _config.yaml
# and _meta.json ARE committed - those are what make a model rebuildable.
# Delete these two lines if you want the ONNX files to travel with the repo.
results/**/deploy/*_traced.pt
results/**/deploy/*.onnx

# Raw Grid5000 job dumps: the console output of a job (one was 23 MB) that
# nothing reads back - the numbers are already in results.csv. logs/ is
# recreated by scripts/run_all.sh and scripts/launch.sh (both mkdir -p).
/OAR.*.stdout
/OAR.*.stderr
/logs/

# LEFTOVER, TO BE MOVED OUT BY HAND. The report was removed from this repository in
# seanetv7, but the folder still exists on disk with UNTRACKED LaTeX sources in it
# (writing that was never committed). This line stops `git add -A` from putting it
# back. Move it out, then delete these three lines:
#     Move-Item ICLR_2025_Report ..\SEANET_Internship_Report_ARCHIVE
/ICLR_2025_Report/

# Crash dumps and stray tool output. Pure noise.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log
core.*

# =============================================================================
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* IGNORED
# =============================================================================
# Do not add these - they are the point of the repo:
#   results/*/SEA_NET/*/results.csv       the numbers themselves
#   results/*/SEA_NET/*/history/          per-epoch train/val loss + accuracy, and the curves
#   results/*/SEA_NET/*/summary.*         the per-model headline
#   results/*/SEA_NET/*/comparison_vs_millet.csv
#   results/*/SEA_NET/*/deploy/*.pt       weights + the config that built them (the ESP32 bundle)
#   results/*/SEA_NET/leaderboard.csv, model_comparison.csv, profile.csv, data_summary.csv
#   results/*/analysis/                   the comparison figures + tables (PNG/CSV/MD, ~11 MB)
#   results/UCR/, results/WebTraffic/     the MILLET paper's PUBLISHED numbers - never regenerate
#   configs/                              every experiment definition
#   guide/                                the documentation

# =============================================================================
# PRIVATE WORKING NOTES
# =============================================================================
# Personal notes, not documentation for anyone else. Everything a reader needs
# is in README.md and guide/.
CLAUDE.md
PROJECT_STATE.md
workflow.md
changes.md